    "Full-song guitar accompaniment prepared from your uploaded recording. Includes the opening verse, both pre-choruses, three choruses, the breakdown and the final repeated refrain. This is a working acoustic adaptation of the studio recording; chord placement and voicings are approximate.",
    "Suggested setup: standard tuning, capo 2. Written shapes Em – D – G sound as F♯m – E – A. The main two-bar pattern is | Em | D G |: hold Em for four beats, then D and G for two beats each. The pre-choruses and breakdown vary the holds. Capo 2 is a convenient arrangement choice; the supplied video shows album artwork and does not establish the artist’s guitar setup.",
    "Try light downstrokes or bass-note-and-brush playing in the verses, then fuller eighth-note strumming in the choruses. Em7 and Gmaj7 can be used as optional colors. These are suggested guitar voicings rather than a note-for-note tab of the recorded instrumental parts.",
    "Lyric review: the opening “Cheap broads” phrase, the pandemic phrase in Verse 2, and the words after “radio” in the pre-choruses remain uncertain. Review markers are retained in the chart. Short pickup words are approximate, and overlapping backing responses are condensed; the breakdown retains the “internet killed the radio” response. The full form is present, including the final chorus and refrain.",
    "Use Watch here or the visible YouTube play-along player for the linked original, where embedding is permitted. You can also select your screen recording in Play-along options; it stays on your device. Repeat can restart the chart, while scroll speed remains manually adjustable rather than synchronized to each lyric."
